From 94c37cf714934a8759e9b77efc0c870bdc77bb5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2398/2409] drm/rockchip: vop2: Assign the AXI ports from the
 whole atomic state

Upstream v2 of the AXI port balancing after the Sashiko review of v1
(sashiko.dev patchset 20261110-vop2-fixes-v1-0-d336e9dd90d3@gmail.com),
carried together with the AXI admission check of
"drm/rockchip: vop2: Reject states that overload an AXI read port":

- The ports are assigned in the atomic check from the whole new state and
  kept in a private object (struct vop2_axi_state); the plane update only
  programs them. Before, the port of a window was chosen in the plane
  update, in plane order, with the per window bookkeeping of the planes
  after it in the same commit still stale.
- The windows that start fetching are assigned busiest first.
- The load counts all planes of the framebuffer (NV12 = 12 bpp, not 8).
- A window switched off keeps its read IDs in use until the frame start
  of its video port (same commit, other video port) or until its commit
  is done (flip_done), instead of releasing them in atomic_disable.
- On a splicing CRTC the window showing the right half is tracked as
  owned by the plane's window (struct vop2_axi_win.owner) and released
  with it. The check runs in vop2_atomic_check() after vop2_splice_check(),
  so the right half windows are known.

It stays its own patch on top of 1301 + 1910: it was written on the VRR and later
VOP2 patches and does not apply at 1301/1910 (upstream: b4/vop2-fixes v2 patch 5).

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
